# The BW-80 keyboard's bench (P5x): the membrane keyboard on J3, its five columns pulled up by
# 47k as on the ZX80, the rows A8-A15 on ties (A9 low: the row of A S D F G; the others high), so
# a key on row 1 reads on its column. For the Session's typing case and the window's screenshot.
part J1 POWER
part J3 BW80KB
part R13 R value=47k
part R14 R value=47k
part R15 R value=47k
part R16 R value=47k
part R17 R value=47k
net KB0 J3.KB0 R13.1
net KB1 J3.KB1 R14.1
net KB2 J3.KB2 R15.1
net KB3 J3.KB3 R16.1
net KB4 J3.KB4 R17.1
net VCC R13.2 R14.2 R15.2 R16.2 R17.2 J3.A8 J3.A10 J3.A11 J3.A12 J3.A13 J3.A14 J3.A15
net GND J3.A9
